pi_error_status":null,"result":"Cycle 93 found why the timing stamps cost about 110 extra lost frames and fixed it. The stamp instrument now passes its perturbation limit, but only narrowly.\n\n- **Cause:** the review (`archive/peer/2026-09-26-c93-h1-stamp-array-copy.md`) refuted the array-copy idea. The real cause was in the stamp DLL: every 1024th stamp flushed its buffer to disk inside the tracking loop's own thread (`tools/t0stamp/t0stamp.c:61-62,74-78`). The six tracking-loop sites all reached that point in the same loop iteration.\n- **Evidence:** in the old stamped runs, the 10 longest tracking-loop periods of each run fell exactly at iterations 1023, 2047, … (108–212 ms each). Periods without a flush had a median of 11.16 ms.\n- **Fix:** `t0stamp` v2 does no disk writes while stamping; it keeps the stamps in memory and writes them when the DLL unloads. It is installed at `claudeDev\\t0stamp.dll` (md5 `b35b398d…`); v1 is kept as `claudeDev\\t0stamp_v1.dll`.\n  - Self-test: 9 pass, 0 fail.\n  - Slowest call: v2 13.6 µs, v1 6.05 ms.\n- **Re-test (8 beads, 120 s, alternating runs):** unstamped 14 / 19 lost frames, stamped with v2 24 / 43. The limit was 53, so the stamps now pass.\n- **Caveat:** the stamped runs still lose about twice as many frames, with two runs per side. So the next measurement keeps unstamped control runs.\n- **Dropped:** the planned build with only the simple-value stamps is cancelled, because its reason is gone.\n- **Retrospective:** it found no rule violation. I accepted its finding that the margin is thin. The plan now has Pre-decided 200 and 201, and STATUS `## NEXT` and `tools/bench/next.json` are updated.\n\n**Next cycle (PD201):** measure per-site timing with v2. The run order is unstamped 11 beads, stamped 11, stamped 15, unstamped 15, stamped 15, stamped 11. From each site's timing at 11 and 15 beads it computes the extra µs per bead. That shows which part of the loop costs more per bead; the current suspect is the For loop #7911 (site 4).\n\nUser decision D-2026-09-26-01 (loop-level timers only) is still open, and the work continues under its recommendation.","ttft_ms":2084,"type":"result","duration_ms":3941530,"uuid":"01b46447-b91c-4c63-bc86-6dbb7b795d18","ttft_stream_ms":1929,"time_to_request_ms":217,"first_content_frame_ms":1929,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
